@prefix img: <https://hexplain.io/ns/image#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/image> skos:scopeNote "Use for image resources and their components. The legacy integer method/color codes preserve profile-specific wire values; they are not universal algorithm or color identifiers."@en .
img:CodeShapes rdfs:label "Code Shapes"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of img:ImageHeader; subjects using img:colorType, img:compressionMethod, img:filterMethod, img:interlaceMethod. img:colorType takes at most one value; each is a literal. Each value of img:compressionMethod is a literal. Each value of img:filterMethod is a literal. Each value of img:interlaceMethod is a literal."@en .
img:ColorProfile skos:definition "A resource describing the color interpretation associated with image samples; its concrete representation is format-specific."@en .
img:Image skos:definition "A raster image considered as a semantic resource, with sample dimensions and interpretation supplied by the imported aspects."@en .
img:ImageHeader skos:definition "A structural component carrying metadata needed to interpret a raster image, separate from its pixel payload."@en .
img:ImageShape rdfs:label "Image Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of img:ImageHeader. acolor:colorSpace takes at most one value; each is an IRI naming an instance of skos:Concept. araster:height takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. araster:width takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. asamp:bitDepth takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0."@en .
img:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
img:PixelData skos:definition "The image component containing encoded or decoded sample values, distinct from header metadata."@en .
img:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using img:colorType, img:compressionMethod, img:filterMethod, img:interlaceMethod. img:colorType takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer). img:compressionMethod takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer). img:filterMethod takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer). img:interlaceMethod takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer)."@en .
img:colorType skos:definition "The legacy integer color-type code carried by an image header. In this vocabulary it preserves a PNG-oriented wire code, not a universal color-space identifier."@en .
img:compressionMethod skos:definition "The legacy integer compression-method code carried by an image header; the code's interpretation is profile-specific."@en .
img:filterMethod skos:definition "The legacy integer filtering-method code carried by an image header; it does not name a general-purpose semantic filter."@en .
img:interlaceMethod skos:definition "The legacy integer interlacing-method code carried by an image header; decode its meaning using the format profile."@en .
